@salmanm I just implemented your solution and it fixed the duplication bug (which occurs whenever you set `prefixTrailingSlash` is set to `both` and it tries to create `HEAD` route for the new route with the trailing slash).

 however it didn't fix the `/prefix/prefix` bug, i think this is because the path (`url`) passed to prepareRoute
 [here](https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/master/lib/route.js#L243) is an empty string, empty strings are not truthy so the `path` property of the `GET` route options object is [used instead](https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/master/lib/route.js#L154) (because options object for the new `HEAD` route is basically created by merging `GET` route options object with additional properties so the final path value of the `GET` route is the path value for the `HEAD` route)
